  "id": "spend-ledger.behavior.exposure-no-escape",
  "kind": "spend-ledger.behavior",
  "milestone": "M6",
  "title": "An exposed payment never expires, so it cannot escape the cap; the 120 s TTL only frees a never-transmitted reservation",
  "spec": ["SPEC §7", "SPEC §3.4", "SPEC §3.4a", "ADR-026"],
  "description": "The P0-1 fix. Two scopes advance past the 120 s reservation TTL. On the first, reservation A1 is exposed (the pre-transmission fence): it never expires, keeps consuming the hourly cap, and a second reserve A2 that would fit only if A1 had dropped is refused with TX402_POLICY_BUDGET. On the second scope the control reservation B1 is NEVER exposed, so at the same instant it has expired and B2 reserves the whole cap again — proving the TTL still applies to exactly the case SPEC §7 says is safe, a reservation that was never transmitted. Under v0.1 both scopes behaved like the control, which is the escape this change closes.",
